<!-- ── §01 Overview ── -->
<section id="s-overview" data-code="overview">
  <div class="section-no">01 — The Capital Problem</div>
  <h2>$100M Is the Ante. Where Does It Go?</h2>
  <p>If you want to train a frontier model today — something competitive with GPT-4 or Llama 3 — you are looking at roughly $100–150M end-to-end, renting compute on the cloud. That number is not a secret: Meta's Llama 3 405B paper details 3.8 × 10<sup>25</sup> FLOPs of pre-training on 16,384 H100 GPUs. Convert that to dollars and the compute bill alone is $80–100M. Add the hidden costs — the data pipeline, the post-training annotation, the engineers — and you cross $100M before your first external demo.</p>
  <p>But what does "roughly $100–150M" actually mean in practice? And how do you sanity-check that number for a model of a different size? This post gives you a reproducible methodology. We'll use Llama 3 405B as the worked example throughout because it's the best-documented frontier model in the public record: Meta released the exact FLOPs count, the GPU type and count, the training token count, and the MFU (model FLOP utilization).</p>
  <p>The goal is a ±50% estimate — precise enough to know whether you need $50M, $150M, or $500M when you're writing your Series A pitch or raising a first fund.</p>

  <div class="vp">
    <div class="vp-head">
      <span class="vp-title">Llama 3 405B — Cost Breakdown by Category</span>
      <span class="vp-hint">Scroll to animate</span>
    </div>
    <div class="vp-body">
      <p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:.875rem">These are best estimates from public data and cloud pricing (June 2026). Pre-training compute dominates at ~60–70% of total cost. The "hidden" costs — storage, annotation, team — add another 20–30%. Modern frontier <em>reasoning</em> models (GPT-o1/o3, Gemini 2.5 Pro, Qwen-3) also add $7–25M in RLVR post-training, shown in red below.</p>
      <div class="waterfall" id="wf-overview">
        <div class="wf-row"><div class="wf-label">Pre-training compute</div><div class="wf-track"><div class="wf-bar" id="wf-0" style="background:var(--purple);left:0%" data-pct="72" data-label="~$80M"><span>~$80M</span></div></div></div>
        <div class="wf-row"><div class="wf-label">Experiments &amp; ablations</div><div class="wf-track"><div class="wf-bar" id="wf-1" style="background:rgba(139,92,246,.6);left:0%" data-pct="11" data-label="~$12M"><span>~$12M</span></div></div></div>
